  body: "# SDA youth transition and qualifying-period distinctions\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe source describes
    a dated transition treating certain SDA days as IB(Y) days and separately sets out SDA’s incapacity and, for
    some claimants, disablement qualifying-period requirements.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe youth transition
    depends on the source’s age, date and continuity/linking conditions. SDA’s qualifying-period treatment of some
    disqualification days differs from IB; identical day counts do not make the regimes interchangeable.\n\n## Inspected
    passages\n\n- [DMG 57005, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 57006, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=6).\n\
    - [DMG 57013, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=9).\n\
    - [DMG 57016, PDF page 9](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=9).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch57`:
    PDF `e5308157f4aed131c245dfd1554a126ad2800f670127de7995f6c643db8ce63b`; extracted pages `5b68aac36596be58528e0c3561d5ef604ec3cf774a61eb2ab93d8639dca9531c`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.506330Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=6
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/ib-youth-overlap-classification
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The historical SDA transition explicitly uses IB(Y), preserving the stated dates and
      conditions.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch57/0006
      quote: "57005   Days of entitlement to SDA in the period 6.4.01 to 5.4.02 are treated as days of\n       \
        \ entitlement to IB(Y) if the claimant\n\n        1.      was aged under 20 on 5.4.01 and\n\n        2.\
        \      continues to be incapable of work (see DMG 57006 where incapacity is not\n                continuous).\n\
        \n        If incapacity continues the person is entitled to IBLT from 6.4.021. IB under this\n        paragraph
        is not reduced by pension payments (See DMG 56135).\n                                                  \
        \                                       1 SS (IB) Regs, reg 19(1)"
      locator: DMG 57005
